{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/borrowingiteratorprotocol\/nextspan(maxcount:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"nextSpan(maxCount:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nextSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s25BorrowingIteratorProtocolP7FailureQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"Span","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s25BorrowingIteratorProtocolP7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:s25BorrowingIteratorProtocolP8nextSpan8maxCounts0E0Vy7ElementQzGSi_t7FailureQzYKF","required":true,"platforms":[{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","name":"iOS","deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","name":"macOS","deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","name":"tvOS","deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","name":"visionOS","deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","name":"watchOS","deprecated":false}],"modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@_lifetime(&self) @_lifetime(self: copy self) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"nextSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxCount"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol\/Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Failure","preciseIdentifier":"s:s25BorrowingIteratorProtocolP7FailureQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/CompatibilitySpan\/Span","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Span","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol\/Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:s25BorrowingIteratorProtocolP7ElementQa"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the underlying type stores its elements in one or more blocks of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contiguous memory, then the returned span typically directly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"addresses one of those buffers. On the other hand, if the underlying type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"materializes its elements on demand, then the returned span addresses"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a temporary buffer managed by the iterator itself. Consequently, the returned","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"span is tied to this particular invocation of "},{"code":"nextSpan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and it cannot","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"survive beyond the next invocation of this method.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the iterator has not yet reached the end of the underlying elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then this method returns a non-empty span of at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements and updates the iterator’s current position to the element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"following the last item in the returned span. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"argument allows callers to avoid getting more items than they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"able to process in one go, simplifying usage, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"avoiding materializing more elements than needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the iterator’s current position is at the end of the container, then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this method returns an empty span without updating the position.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This method can be used to efficiently process the items of a container","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in bulk, by directly iterating over its piecewise contiguous pieces of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var it = items.makeBorrowingIterator()","while true {","  let span = it.nextSpan(maxCount: .max)","  if span.isEmpty { break }","  \/\/ Process items in `span`","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The spans returned by this method are not guaranteed to be disjunct.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iterators that materialize elements on demand typically reuse the same","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"buffer over and over again; and even some proper containers may link to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single storage chunk (or parts of a storage chunk) multiple times, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example to repeat their contents."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol\/nextSpan(maxCount:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a span over the next group of elements that are ready to by visited,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"up to the specifed maximum."}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/BorrowingIteratorProtocol/Failure":{"required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol\/Failure","title":"Failure","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/borrowingiteratorprotocol\/failure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Failure"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Never","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/CompatibilitySpan/Span":{"abstract":[{"code":"Span<Element>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents a contiguous region of memory","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which contains initialized instances of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"